  "title": "iEEG_visual",
  "description": "This dataset contains intracranial EEG (ECoG) recordings from two subjects performing a visual fixation task involving high-contrast gratings and noise pattern stimuli. The data were collected to investigate stimulus-dependent gamma oscillations and the relationship between neuronal synchrony, BOLD responses, and local field potentials in human visual cortex. The dataset supports two published studies on visual cortical electrophysiology.",
  "methods_description": "Subjects viewed images spanning approximately 25x25 degrees of visual angle on a computer screen while fixating on a dot that changed color at random times. Stimuli included high-contrast vertical gratings at various spatial frequencies and noise patterns with different spectral power distributions. ECoG data were recorded and stored in BrainVision format.",
